  m_Name: PokedexSnakeion 1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  entryId: snake
  commonName: Corn Snake
  scientificName: Pantherophis guttatus
  icon: {fileID: 10904, guid: 0000000000000000f000000000000000, type: 0}
  category: ' Reptile'
  habitat: Arid Deserts & Scrublands
  height: 90 - 150 cm
  weight: 150 - 450 g
  diet: Carnivore
  rarity: Uncommon
  shortDescription: A slender, non-venomous desert snake with dark saddle-shaped
    blotches rimmed in black along a muted brown-red body, built for slipping between
    rocks and burrows.
  behaviorNotes: Mostly crepuscular and nocturnal, avoiding peak heat by sheltering
    in rodent burrows or beneath flat rocks; an efficient constrictor that ambushes
    small mammals near burrow entrances.
  observationTips: Look for faint trail marks in loose sand near burrow openings
    at dusk; its blotched pattern breaks up its outline against rocky, sun-bleached
    terrain.
  funFact: Its blotch pattern is a Batesian mimic of venomous coral-adjacent species,
    deterring predators without producing any venom itself.
  facts:
  - Like almost all scorpions, they glow an eerie, bright cyan-blue color when exposed
    to ultraviolet light due to fluorescent chemicals in their exoskeleton.
  - They do not rely on eyesight to hunt; instead, they use tiny, specialized sensory
    hairs on their legs to detect microscopic ground vibrations made by moving insects.
  - They are exceptionally resilient to extreme heat and dehydration, capable of
    slowing their metabolic rate to survive on just a few insects per year.
